          %h3#boundary_conditions__dbranes Boundary conditions / D-branes
          %p (…)
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
          %p
            For exhaustive details on D-branes in 2-dimensional rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
            see the references given at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FFRS-formalism"}> FFRS-formalism
              \.
          %p
            A classical text describing how the physics way to think of D-branes for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
            leads to seeing that they are objects in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+categories"} derived categories
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            for the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
              ,
              %em D-Branes on Calabi-Yau Manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0403166"}> arXiv
              )
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"}> Michael Douglas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    D-branes, Categories and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
